  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Wednesday)\nIssued at 211 PM MST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nCurrent upper air analysis and water vapor imagery shows \nshortwave ridging over the region. Visible satellite depicts high\nclouds over northeastern WY and far western SD with low clouds \nand patchy fog dissipating over central SD. Sfc obs around the \nregion show southerly winds and temperatures in the 40s to low \n50s. Shortwave ridging will continue to influence the weather \nthrough tomorrow. Thanksgiving Day should be dry with partly \ncloudy skies and highs in the upper 40s to low 50s.\n\nOur next system moves through the area during the day Friday. An \nupper low will pass to the north of the CWA with an attendant cold\nfront pushing through the area Friday morning. This front will \nbring breezy west to northwest winds (max gusts of 45-55 mph) to \nnorthwestern SD for Friday afternoon. Light rain/snow will move \nthrough northeastern WY into the Black Hills and southwestern SD \nSaturday. Deterministic models are coming into better agreement as\nto the path of the system on Saturday. Current runs indicate the \ngreatest QPF (around 0.05-0.25\") over northeastern WY into the \nBlack Hills and southern SD. Temperatures over northeastern WY and\nthe Black Hills should be cold enough for snow with rain over \nsouthern SD. Any snow accumulations should be minor. Northwest \nwinds will also pick up again on Saturday with gusts again \nreaching 45 to 55 mph over northwestern SD.",
